A securitisation holds a collateral pool with par balance $63,800,000. It has issued a senior tranche A of $49,400,000 paying 2% interest per period on its outstanding balance, and a junior tranche B of $8,200,000 paying 5% interest per period (B's principal is not repaid during the two periods). Equity receives whatever is left. In each of two periods, the pool collects interest of 8% of its par balance at the start of the period plus scheduled principal of $2,900,000. At the end of each period, par falls by the scheduled principal and by that period's defaults (period 1: $7,900,000; period 2: $4,000,000), with no recoveries. Each period's collections are paid in this order: (1) senior interest on tranche A's balance at the start of the period; (2) the overcollateralisation (OC) test: if end-of-period par divided by tranche A's balance is below 125%, cash is diverted to repay tranche A principal, exactly the amount that brings the ratio back to 125% (or all remaining cash if that is less); (3) junior interest on tranche B, where any shortfall is lost, not carried forward; (4) everything left goes to equity. Tranche A's balance falls only through OC diversions. What is the total cash received by junior tranche B over both periods? Give the amount in whole dollars. Reply with only the number.